{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_5wzklu4o","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Feature: build an assistant comparison summary\n2\t\n3\tImplement the comparison-summary feature in these files:\n4\t\n5\t- `benchmark/fixtures/T3-comparison-summary/summarize-assistants.mjs`\n6\t- `benchmark/fixtures/T3-comparison-summary/render-comparison-table.mjs`\n7\t\n8\tAlso add at least two meaningful `node:test` cases to:\n9\t\n10\t- `benchmark/fixtures/T3-comparison-summary/student-tests.mjs`\n11\t\n12\tDo not edit the committed `comparison-summary.test.mjs` suite.\n13\t\n14\t## `summarizeAssistants(runs)` contract\n15\t\n16\t1. Throw `TypeError` when `runs` is not an array.\n17\t2. A run is eligible only when `status === \"complete\"`,\n18\t   `acceptance_status === \"pass\"`, and `comparison_eligible !== false`.\n19\t3. Validate eligible runs. `run_id` and `assistant` must be non-empty strings;\n20\t   `score` must be a finite number from 0 through 100; `elapsed_ms` must be a\n21\t   finite number greater than or equal to zero. Throw `TypeError` for invalid\n22\t   eligible data. Invalid fields on an ineligible run do not matter.\n23\t4. Group eligible runs by the exact, case-sensitive `assistant` value.\n24\t5. Return one object per assistant with exactly these fields:\n25\t   `assistant`, `run_count`, `best_score`, `best_run_id`, and\n26\t   `median_elapsed_ms`.\n27\t6. The best run has the highest score. Break a score tie using the lower elapsed\n28\t   time, then the lexicographically smaller `run_id` using normal JavaScript\n29\t   string comparison.\n30\t7. Median time uses all eligible runs for the assistant after a numeric sort. For\n31\t   an even count, average the two middle values.\n32\t8. Sort the returned summaries by `assistant` using normal JavaScript string\n33\t   comparison. Do not mutate the input array or its records.\n34\t\n35\t## `renderComparisonTable(summaries)` contract\n36\t\n37\t1. Throw `TypeError` when `summaries` is not an array or a summary has invalid\n38\t   fields. `assistant` and `best_run_id` must be non-empty strings; `run_count`\n39\t   must be a positive integer; `best_score` must be a finite number from 0\n40\t   through 100; and `median_elapsed_ms` must be a finite number greater than or\n41\t   equal to zero.\n42\t2. Preserve the supplied summary order.\n43\t3. Return this exact Markdown header:\n44\t\n45\t   `| Assistant | Runs | Best score | Best run | Median time |`\n46\t\n47\t   followed by:\n48\t\n49\t   `|---|---:|---:|---|---:|`\n50\t4. Render median milliseconds as seconds with exactly three decimal places.\n51\t5. Escape `|` in assistant names and run IDs as `\\|`.\n52\t6. For an empty array, render the two header lines, a blank line, and\n53\t   `_No eligible runs._`.\n54\t\n55\t## Boundaries and verification\n56\t\n57\t- Change only the three files named at the top of this prompt.\n58\t- Do not install dependencies, use the network, commit, or alter generated runs.\n59\t- Add at least two real tests; do not use `test.todo`, `test.skip`, or placeholder\n60\t  assertions.\n61\t- Run:\n62\t  `node --test benchmark/fixtures/T3-comparison-summary/comparison-summary.test.mjs benchmark/fixtures/T3-comparison-summary/student-tests.mjs`\n63\t\n64\tIn the final response, summarize the design, edge cases covered by your added\n65\ttests, and the verification result.\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1da5eca0-d58c-4774-8d48-41166d9f2452","uuid":"8ed2239b-2699-430f-a7d4-327efbaf8fa1","timestamp":"2026-08-23T00:07:16.427Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-KFa75N/checkout/benchmark/tasks/T3-comparison-summary/prompt.md","content":"# Feature: build an assistant comparison summary\n\nImplement the comparison-summary feature in these files:\n\n- `benchmark/fixtures/T3-comparison-summary/summarize-assistants.mjs`\n- `benchmark/fixtures/T3-comparison-summary/render-comparison-table.mjs`\n\nAlso add at least two meaningful `node:test` cases to:\n\n- `benchmark/fixtures/T3-comparison-summary/student-tests.mjs`\n\nDo not edit the committed `comparison-summary.test.mjs` suite.\n\n## `summarizeAssistants(runs)` contract\n\n1. Throw `TypeError` when `runs` is not an array.\n2. A run is eligible only when `status === \"complete\"`,\n   `acceptance_status === \"pass\"`, and `comparison_eligible !== false`.\n3. Validate eligible runs. `run_id` and `assistant` must be non-empty strings;\n   `score` must be a finite number from 0 through 100; `elapsed_ms` must be a\n   finite number greater than or equal to zero. Throw `TypeError` for invalid\n   eligible data. Invalid fields on an ineligible run do not matter.\n4. Group eligible runs by the exact, case-sensitive `assistant` value.\n5. Return one object per assistant with exactly these fields:\n   `assistant`, `run_count`, `best_score`, `best_run_id`, and\n   `median_elapsed_ms`.\n6. The best run has the highest score. Break a score tie using the lower elapsed\n   time, then the lexicographically smaller `run_id` using normal JavaScript\n   string comparison.\n7. Median time uses all eligible runs for the assistant after a numeric sort. For\n   an even count, average the two middle values.\n8. Sort the returned summaries by `assistant` using normal JavaScript string\n   comparison. Do not mutate the input array or its records.\n\n## `renderComparisonTable(summaries)` contract\n\n1. Throw `TypeError` when `summaries` is not an array or a summary has invalid\n   fields. `assistant` and `best_run_id` must be non-empty strings; `run_count`\n   must be a positive integer; `best_score` must be a finite number from 0\n   through 100; and `median_elapsed_ms` must be a finite number greater than or\n   equal to zero.\n2. Preserve the supplied summary order.\n3. Return this exact Markdown header:\n\n   `| Assistant | Runs | Best score | Best run | Median time |`\n\n   followed by:\n\n   `|---|---:|---:|---|---:|`\n4. Render median milliseconds as seconds with exactly three decimal places.\n5. Escape `|` in assistant names and run IDs as `\\|`.\n6. For an empty array, render the two header lines, a blank line, and\n   `_No eligible runs._`.\n\n## Boundaries and verification\n\n- Change only the three files named at the top of this prompt.\n- Do not install dependencies, use the network, commit, or alter generated runs.\n- Add at least two real tests; do not use `test.todo`, `test.skip`, or placeholder\n  assertions.\n- Run:\n  `node --test benchmark/fixtures/T3-comparison-summary/comparison-summary.test.mjs benchmark/fixtures/T3-comparison-summary/student-tests.mjs`\n\nIn the final response, summarize the design, edge cases covered by your added\ntests, and the verification result.\n","numLines":66,"startLine":1,"totalLines":66}}}
