{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_03ab1edd775f33026c0617bb","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All checks pass. Only the three permitted files changed. Here's the summary.\n\n## Design\n\n**`summarize-assistants.mjs`** — `summarizeAssistants(runs)`:\n- Throws `TypeError` for non-array input up front.\n- `isEligible()` treats a run as eligible only when `status === \"complete\"`, `acceptance_status === \"pass\"`, and `comparison_eligible !== false` (so a missing field is eligible, only an explicit `false` excludes). It guards `null`/primitives so invalid ineligible records are skipped, not crashed on.\n- `validateEligibleRun()` enforces the data contract per eligible run: non-empty string `run_id`/`assistant`, finite `score` in `[0, 100]`, finite `elapsed_ms >= 0`, throwing `TypeError` otherwise.\n- Groups by exact case-sensitive `assistant` via a `Map`. For each group, the best run is selected by highest `score`, then lower `elapsed_ms`, then lexicographically smaller `run_id` (`<`). Median uses a numeric sort of a copy (no mutation) — odd count takes the middle value, even count averages the two middles.\n- Summaries carry exactly the five contract fields, sorted by `assistant` with normal JS string comparison. The input array and its records are never mutated.\n\n**`render-comparison-table.mjs`** — `renderComparisonTable(summaries)`:\n- Throws `TypeError` for non-array input and for any summary failing field validation (`run_count` must be a positive integer, `assistant`/`best_run_id` non-empty strings, `best_score` finite in `[0,100]`, `median_elapsed_ms` finite ≥ 0).\n- Preserves supplied order, emits the exact header/divider, renders median ms as seconds with `.toFixed(3)` (e.g. `1.250 s`), escapes `|` → `\\|` in assistant names and run IDs, and renders the empty-state (header + divider + blank line + `_No eligible runs._`).\n\n## Edge cases covered by the added student tests\n\n1. **Case-sensitive grouping + run_id tie-break + even-count median** — `OpenCode` vs `opencode` grouped separately; two runs tied on score *and* elapsed time resolve by smaller `run_id`; a 4-run even median averages the middle two (150); input order is asserted unchanged (immutability).\n2. **Validation isolation** — non-array input throws; an *eligible* run with out-of-range score throws; an *ineligible* run carrying invalid fields is ignored; the remaining valid run still summarizes correctly.\n3. **Renderer order + escaping + seconds formatting** — supplied order is preserved even when not alphabetical; pipes escaped in both columns; `1250 ms → 1.250 s` and `500 ms → 0.500 s`.\n4. **Renderer validation** — non-array input and each invalid field (`run_count: 0`, `best_score: 101`, negative `median_elapsed_ms`, empty `assistant`) throw `TypeError`.\n\n## Verification\n\n```\nnode --test benchmark/fixtures/T3-comparison-summary/comparison-summary.test.mjs benchmark/fixtures/T3-comparison-summary/student-tests.mjs\n```\n```\n✔ 8 tests / 8 pass / 0 fail / 0 skipped\n```\nThis includes the 4 committed tests (now passing against the new implementation) and the 4 new student tests. `git status` confirms only the three allowed files changed; nothing was committed, installed, or networked."}],"usage":{"input_tokens":28012,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1da5eca0-d58c-4774-8d48-41166d9f2452","uuid":"719c3ed0-1178-47cb-a020-969646d56ea1","timestamp":"2026-08-23T00:08:05.249Z"}
